\[
\begin{align*}
3x + 4y - 12z &= 10, \quad \text{(1)} \\
-2x - 3y + 9z &= -4, \quad \text{(2)}
\end{align*}
\]

we will use the method of elimination. First, we will eliminate \(y\) by making the coefficients of \(y\) in both equations equal in magnitude but opposite in sign.

1. **Multiply equation (1) by 3 and equation (2) by 4 to align the coefficients of \(y\):**

\[
\begin{align*}
3(3x + 4y - 12z) &= 3(10) \\
4(-2x - 3y + 9z) &= 4(-4)
\end{align*}
\]

This gives us:

\[
\begin{align*}
9x + 12y - 36z &= 30, \quad \text{(3)} \\
-8x - 12y + 36z &= -16, \quad \text{(4)}
\end{align*}
\]

2. **Add equations (3) and (4) to eliminate \(y\):**

\[
\begin{align*}
(9x + 12y - 36z) + (-8x - 12y + 36z) &= 30 + (-16) \\
9x - 8x + 12y - 12y - 36z + 36z &= 14 \\
x &= 14
\end{align*}
\]

Thus, the value of \(x\) is \(\boxed{14}\).

